# agent-workbench.env -- OPTIONAL data-root overrides for the `deploy`
# subcommand. No secrets live here. Copy, edit, then `. agent-workbench.env`
# before `agent-workbench deploy up`, or export the vars yourself.

# bd (beads) board hub. FUNCTIONAL: read directly by the `hub` / `deploy`
# Python code, honored everywhere.
BEADS_HUB_DIR=$HOME/.beads-hub

# Knowledgebase vault and artifact artifact root.
#
# NOT a functional override once the containers are running. The quadlets
# bind %h-relative host paths (systemd's %h = the real $HOME), and quadlet
# does not do arbitrary env substitution, so setting these does NOT move
# where the CONTAINERIZED kb-serve / artifact service read and write. They only
# affect code paths that read the env var directly. To
# actually relocate the containerized data roots, edit the quadlet
# Volume=/Environment= lines. See docs/agent-workbench-hardening-plan.md (H3).
KB_HOME=$HOME/.knowledgebase
ARTIFACTS_HOME=$HOME/.local/share/artifacts

# kb-serve's LLM-enrichment secrets are NOT here -- see
# scripts/kb-container/kb.env.example and copy it to $KB_HOME/kb.env.
